    "question": "Ben has 8 apples more than Phillip does. Tom has three eighths as many apples at Ben has. If Phillip has 40 apples, how many apples does Tom have?",
    "gold": "18",
    "answer": "Ben has 40+8 = <<40+8=48>>48 apples.\nThere are 48/8 = <<48/8=6>>6 apples in every eighth.\nTom has 6*3 = <<6*3=18>>18 apples.\n#### 18"
  },
  "generation": {
    "text": "To determine how many apples Tom has, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Identify how many apples Ben has.\n2. Use the information about Ben's apples to find out how many apples Tom has.\n\nStep 1: Determine how many apples Ben has.\nWe know that Ben has 8 apples more than Phillip. Since Phillip has 40 apples, we can calculate the number of apples Ben has as follows:\n\\[ \\text{Number of apples Ben has} = 40 + 8 = 48 \\]\n\nStep 2: Determine how many apples Tom has.\nWe know that Tom has three eighths as many apples as Ben. Since Ben has 48 apples, we can calculate the number of apples Tom has as follows:\n\\[ \\text{Number of apples Tom has} = \\frac{3}{8} \\times 48 = \\frac{3 \\times 48}{8} = \\frac{144}{8} = 18 \\]\n\nTherefore, the number of apples Tom has is \\(\\boxed{18}\\).",
